    businessChallenge: "Most SMEs struggle to maintain consistent marketing content output. Founders write posts themselves between other responsibilities, quality is uneven, and the pace drops to zero during busy seasons. Hiring agencies is expensive and slow. Internal marketing staff spend most of their time on repetitive drafting tasks — product descriptions, social posts, email campaigns, promotional messages — leaving no bandwidth for strategy or creative direction. For businesses competing with larger, better-resourced brands, inconsistent marketing presence directly impacts customer acquisition.",
